<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Władysław of Opole</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1225–1281</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Władysław I of Opole</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Władysław of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opole">Opole</a> was a Piast Duke of Opole and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raciborz">Racibórz</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-silesia">Upper Silesia</a> from 1246 to 1281. He founded towns under German law and allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> against the Hungarians. On his death in 1281 the duchy was divided among his four sons, Bolko I receiving Opole on the Oder.</p></div>
